WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.069
-Our next guest is an activist
author and six-time NBA champion

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.139
as well as the league's all-time
leading scorer.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
His documentary,
"Fight the Power:

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Movements
That Changed America"

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:12.312
premieres on the History Channel
June 19th.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:12.946 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-After meeting Dr. King
and, you know,

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
really getting into
his philosophy,

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.086 line:92%
I saw where the power was in it.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
It really embarrasses
and totally takes the face awa

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
from oppressors
when they're shown

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.597 line:92%
to be the bullies that they are.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Kareem.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.636 line:92%
-Nice to talk to you, Seth

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:40.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is a documentary
about the history of activism.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were someone
who embraced it very early

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your career where it wa
maybe less commonplace

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:48.915 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than we see it now.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:53.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does activism in sport
today reflect to what

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were going through
when you were getting started?

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, when I was
getting started,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had several great examples
in front of me.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
Muhammad Ali, Bill Russell
Jackie Robinson,

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:12.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of whom were people that
I met and I admired them

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:17.010 size:81% position:41%
for what they achieved
as athletes but also

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.581
for the strength and dignity
that they showed the country

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.650 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as black Americans.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
That made me feel proud to b
a black American,

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's something
that inspired me.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when Muhammad Ali got on
the wrong side of the law

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he opposed
the Vietnam War,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.596 line:92%
I was going to be there for him.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:41.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, because I knew tha
his insights into it

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
were accurate
and that what he felt

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.539 line:92%
was pretty much on the money

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned in the clip tha
you met Martin Luther King

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a picture of you
with him here.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:56.316 line:92%
What was that experience like?

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.650 line:92%
-Oh, that was incredible.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I got to ask --
I was involved in

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:07.360
a summer mentoring worksho
and involved in journalism

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.200
So I got to cover Dr. King's
address to the mentoring group

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the national press
that followed him.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
He'd been elected
Man of the Year in 1963,

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.743 line:92%
and this was summer of 1964.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:28.481
You know, this was at a time
when I more or less kind o

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.451 size:78% position:39%
related to Malcolm X
more so than Dr. King

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.254 line:92%
because you get emotional

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.955 size:88% position:44%
when you see your people
abused and everything.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:40.927
I wanted to retaliate, but
Dr. King helped us understan

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
that by nonviolence,
we're able to expose the bully

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
for who he is and just make it
impossible for his agenda

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.273 size:81% position:41% line:92%
to be taken seriously,

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:56.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this eventually worked for
black Americans.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:01.181
But it took a lot of courage
and patience and, you know

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.783 line:92%
just that one incident helped me

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
get around
to understanding that.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:09.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wrote about
the Black Lives Matter momen

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.492
that happened last summer
and about how it gave you

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:15.428
tears of hope, but often
tears of hope can turn int

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
tears of rage
and tears of frustration.

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:23.636
Looking back at last summer, d
you have optimism in so far as

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.704 line:92%
what direction we're headed?

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think last summer
really gave us a moment

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
of being able
to understand each other.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:35.949
After people saw what happened
to George Floyd and realized

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:40.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this is what black
Americans had been speaking of

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:44.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
for 400 years, it probably was
a moment of insight

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.593 line:92%
for Americans of all stripes

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:51.164
And I think that has given u
a chance to actually deal with

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
the issue of racism
and the denial of equal rights

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was actually fortunate
that people saw that

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:09.782
because now, no one can deny
something that is that obvious

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:14.354
No one can deny that, and
think we will be better of

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:18.758
because of the doors and bridges
that were built

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the doors that were opened
by that moment.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wrote about that.
You've written several essays.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.433
You've written works of fiction.
You've written for television.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:31.104
Did you know writing was a skill
you had around the same time

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.906 size:84% position:42%
you realized basketball
was a skill you had?

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.776
-Well, you know, I was
an English major at UCLA,

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:40.280
but you don't know how far
you're going to get with it.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also dabbled in history,
so, you know, I guess

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.487
joining the two discipline
really has been something

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.356 line:92%
that has given me a voice.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:54.127
-One of your writing credits
people might be less aware o

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:57.897
is that you wrote for the
television show "Veronica Mars."

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was that experience?
-Yes, I did.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:04.170
Actually, it was really good
for me as a writer because

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
it teaches you how you have to
structure the story

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how to make sense
from one end to the other

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:15.882
or people will lose interest
and, you know, people won'

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
finish your book
or finish watching your movie.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:22.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I found it was
a great learning experience.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.123 line:92%
Glad to see it on my résumé.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:27.360
-The NBA announced this year
that they are going to award

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Kareem Abdul-Jabbar
Social Justice Champion Award.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.500
How does it feel, you know, fo
everything you did on the court,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.670
to have an award named for
the work you did off of it

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a great honor to hav
an award that rewards activism

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:49.949
I think the young men in the NBA
will, you know, use these awards

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
to figure out good things to d
with them and help continu

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
to spread the word about
what's right and what's wrong.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:04.897
So this will give a lot of
people the incentive to se

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
what they can do to improv
their communities,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think it will bear
a lot of good fruit.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Finally, I do want to
ask about --

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.441
I think this maybe was
the first time I saw you.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think before I even saw yo
play basketball,

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:18.845 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I saw you in "Airplane!"

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:22.281
And then I was very impresse
that someone that funny wa

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
also as good at basketball
as you were.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.322
Do people still approach you
and ask you about this movie

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
I've lost all my hair

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they don't recognize me
anymore.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But you know what's funny?

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
The guy in that picture,
the kid, I ran into his wife

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.133 line:92%
You know, he's in his 40s now,

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I ran into his wife
in the airport,

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.437 line:92%
and I was like, "What? Who?"

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.671 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Well, it's great.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's nice to know
people still recognize you

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:55.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
for that great effort
as well as everything else

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.550 size:78% position:39%
and thank you so much
for making the time

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.152 line:92%
and being with us today, Kareem.

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.119 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Great talking to you.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:03.656
-"Fight the Power: The Movements
That Changed America" premiere

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the History Channel
June 19th.

